{"Openness":          {"score": 3, "behavioral_evidence": "He adapts his request from an exchange to a new custom suit when an immediate exchange is impossible, showing flexibility within practical limits. 'Can you please provide me with the measurements and fabric for a different suit?'"},
  "Conscientiousness": {"score": 4, "behavioral_evidence": "He consistently pursues his goal of obtaining a suitable garment for an important upcoming trial, persistently seeking solutions despite repeated rejections. 'Then you'll have to help me. We need a solution. This suit isn't suitable. I've changed my mind, I don't want it anymore.'"},
  "Extraversion":      {"score": 3, "behavioral_evidence": "He is direct and articulate in his communication, initiating conversation and clearly stating his purpose and evolving requests. 'Ah, good day to you. I trust you are the master tailor, Mr. Charles Keane? My name is Abraham Lincoln.'"},
  "Agreeableness":     {"score": 3, "behavioral_evidence": "He is polite and acknowledges the assistant's position ('I understand your position') but is also assertive and unyielding in pursuing his own needs and challenging the shop's policy. 'I understand your position, but this is a problem. The suit is of inferior quality and doesn't meet my expectations.'"},
  "Neuroticism":       {"score": 2, "behavioral_evidence": "He maintains a calm, composed, and rational demeanor throughout the interaction, even when his requests are repeatedly denied and he describes the situation as a 'problem.'"}
}
